    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="0527" n="519" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg519"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.115 Panay/211: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-29T10:00:00+09:00">December 29, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 29—2:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>694. Department’s 381, December 28, 5 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d674-f1"/> I
                    immediately consulted Prince Tokugawa<anchor n="3" xml:id="d674-f2"/> with
                    regard to the disposal of donations received in connection with the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Panay</hi> incident and am in constant touch with the
                    officers of the America-Japan Society who have agreed to handle the matter and
                    are now discussing the most helpful way to use the funds in the interests of
                    Japanese-American friendship. They now have under consideration the possible
                    endowment of a hospital bed but it is difficult to reach a decision until the
                    final approximate amount of contributed money can be ascertained. I have urged
                    the <pb facs="0528" n="520" xml:id="pg520"/> importance of an early decision as
                    well as a public statement by Prince Tokugawa as soon as the plans can be
                    settled.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d674-f1" n="2" xml:id="d674-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; see Department’s telegram No. 361, December 18, 6 p.m., <ref
                        target="frus1931-41v01#pg_530"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >i</hi>, p. 530</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d674-f2" n="3" xml:id="d674-f2-content">
                <p>President of the Japanese House of Peers and of the America-Japan Society.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
